<tNVSE>
  <fonts>
    <!--
      Configuration reference

      Only listed font IDs are configured. If an ID appears more than once,
      the last entry wins.

      <font> attributes

      id
        Required positive game font slot. Common slots:
        1 = Glow_Monofonto_Large
        2 = Monofonto_Large
        3 = Glow_Monofonto_Medium
        4 = Monofonto_VeryLarge02_Dialogs2
        5 = Fixedsys_Comp_uniform_width
        6 = Glow_Monofonto_VL_dialogs
        7 = Baked-in_Monofonto_Large
        8 = Glow_Futura_Caps_Large
        With JIP LN NVSE, registered extended slots 10 through 89 are also
        supported; slot 9 is invalid. Stewie Tweaks registers its menu font in
        slot 42 through JIP's SetFontFile command.

      pixelSize
        Font size in pixels; must be greater than 0.
      tracking
        Additional character spacing in pixels. Default: 0.
      fixedWidth
        Logical cell width in pixels. 0 selects proportional advances;
        positive values select a fixed cell. Default: 0.
      scaleX / scaleY
        Horizontal and vertical glyph scale; must be greater than 0. Default: 1.
      embolden
        Outline emboldening in pixels; must be 0 or greater. Default: 0.
      slant
        Slant angle in degrees from -45 through 45. Default: 0.
      baselineOffset
        Final per-glyph vertical adjustment in pixels, applied after automatic
        visual alignment; may be fractional or negative. Default: 0.
      verticalMetrics
        "freetype" derives the line box from configured faces and is the
        default. "original" preserves the original .fnt line box. Automatic
        singleByte/doubleByte alignment measures hinted visible glyph ink at
        the configured FreeType source-resolution scale without creating
        separate line baselines.
      baseline
        Fallout line rise/ascent in pixels. 0 derives or inherits it according
        to verticalMetrics; a positive value overrides it. Default: 0.
      unicodeLineBreaking
        0 preserves the legacy space, ~, and hard-wrap rules. 1 decodes the
        current font text code page and adds libunibreak UAX #14 opportunities
        without splitting DBCS units. Default: 0.
      prewarm
        "none" disables startup prewarming and is the default. "common"
        prepares all valid single-byte units plus the complete GB2312
        double-byte set under CP936; other code pages prepare up to 7000
        common double-byte units. "codepage" prepares the configured code-page
        profile (complete GBK under CP936). When the multibyte font hook is
        disabled, both modes prepare only the 224 Windows-1252 units 0x20-0xFF.
      effectQuality
        "fast", "balanced", or "high". Default: "balanced".
      fontColor
        Optional fill-color override in #RRGGBB format.
      fontAlpha
        Alpha used with fontColor, clamped from 0 through 1. Default: 1.

      <singleByte> and <doubleByte>

      singleByte handles valid one-byte units; doubleByte handles valid DBCS
      pairs. FreeType-only mode is always Windows-1252 and therefore routes
      every byte through singleByte, regardless of configured uiEncoding.
      Each byte-class node may override:
        pixelSize, tracking, fixedWidth, scaleX, scaleY, embolden, slant,
        baselineOffset
      Unspecified values inherit from <font>. Other <font> attributes and all
      effect nodes apply to the complete font ID.

      Font files

      <face path="..." index="0"/>
        Required primary font for each resolved byte class.
      <fallback path="..." index="0"/>
        Optional fallback; multiple entries are tried in document order.
      path
        Absolute or relative to FalloutNV.exe; either slash style is accepted.
      index
        Non-negative face index for TTF/OTF/TTC/OTC files. Default: 0.

      A face chain directly under <font> is inherited by both byte classes.
      A byte class containing any face/fallback child replaces the inherited
      chain and must contain a valid <face>.

      Effects

      Every effect node accepts enabled, colorMode="fixed|fill",
      color="#RRGGBB", and alpha="0..1". colorMode defaults to fixed: the
      configured color is used independently from the live Tile RGB. fill
      tracks the body color and ignores the effect color's RGB; alpha remains
      effect-specific in both modes.
      A present node defaults to enabled; an absent node is disabled. Default
      color is #000000 and default alpha is 1.

      <glow colorMode="fill" inner="0" outer="4" power="2"/>
        inner: full-intensity distance. Default: 0.
        outer: nominal falloff radius; must be greater than inner when enabled.
          The shader feathers the final cutoff by the current pixel footprint.
        power: positive exponential falloff coefficient; larger values fade
          faster. Default: 2.
        width: legacy alias for outer; do not specify both.

      <outline width="1" softness="0.5"/>
        width: positive outline width when enabled.
        softness: non-negative edge transition. Default: 0.5.

      <shadow x="1" y="1" blur="0" power="2"
              includeGlow="1" includeOutline="1"/>
        x / y: signed offsets. Default: 0.
        blur: non-negative blur radius. Default: 0.
        power: positive falloff exponent. Default: 2.
        includeGlow / includeOutline: when blur is 0, copy the currently
          enabled glow or outline coverage into the offset shadow mask. The
          copied coverage keeps the source effect alpha but uses shadow color.
          Both default to 0 and are ignored for blurred shadows.
    -->

